    "text": "Step 2: The cross product $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ can be computed using the determinant formula for the cross product of two vectors. This gives us:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ x & y & z \\end{vmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\cdot (z - y) - 1 \\cdot (x - z) \\\\ 1 \\cdot (x - z) - 1 \\cdot (y - x) \\\\ 1 \\cdot (y - x) - 1 \\cdot (x - y) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} z - y - x + z \\\\ x - z - y + x \\\\ y - x - x + y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2z - x - y \\\\ 2x - y - z \\\\ 2y - 2x \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nSetting this equal to $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, we get three equations:\n\\[\n2z - x - y = 1,\n\\]\n\\[\n2x - y - z = -2,\n\\]\n\\[\n2y - 2x = 1.\n\\]"
